usal maintenance paid or received in the present or other cases (Guidelines II.A, II.C-D, III).","modelText":"Rows are $50 apart up to $2,000 and $100 apart from $2,000 to $18,000. For income amounts not shown, income is rounded to the nearest amount on the schedule (Guidelines VI.J.2). Use the schedule for the total number of children; read each child's amount in its age column (age at nearest birthday) and add them (Guidelines IV.B, IV.D.2).","sharedText":"Parenting time adjustment: if the child spends 35% or more of its time with the nonresidential parent the court decides whether to adjust; the table gives 10% (35-39%), 20% (40-44%), 30% (45-49%) of that parent's share (worksheet line E.1.a: % x Line D.5) (Guidelines IV.H.2). Extended parenting time of 14+ consecutive days may reduce support by up to 50% (IV.H.3). Equal parenting time (discretionary): shared expense formula or direct expense formula = (higher share - lower share) / 2 plus 7% (combined income <= $4,690), 10.5% (> $4,690 and < $8,125) or 15% (>= $8,125) of the gross child support obligation (Guidelines VI.B-F).","addOnsText":"Work-related child care costs are added and shared proportionately (worksheet line G; Guidelines IV.J). Health, dental, vision and orthodontic premiums for the child are added and shared proportionately (worksheet line F; Guidelines IV.I). Each parent's proportionate obligation = gross support share + parenting time/shared residency adjustment + share of premiums + share of work-related child care (Guidelines IV.C).","lowIncomeText":"Ability to pay: subtract the current federal poverty guideline for a household of one from the parent's child support income; support owed is the lesser of that and the guideline amount, or a best-interest amount if the available income is lower (Guidelines VI.G). The schedules note the 2023 poverty guideline for one person as $1,250 per month (rounded up to $50).","emancipation":{"text":"Support ends at 18 unless agreed otherwise; if the child is still in high school it continues to June 30 of the school year in which the child turned 18, and on motion may continue through the school year in which the child turns 19 (K.S.A. 23-3001(b)).","url":"https://www.ksrevisor.gov/statutes/chapters/ch23/023_030_0001.html"},"scheduleText":"Rows are $50 apart up to $2,000 and $100 apart from $2,000 to $18,000. For income amounts not shown, income is rounded to the nearest amount on the schedule (Guidelines VI.J.2). Use the schedule for the total number of children; read each child's amount in its age column (age at nearest birthday) and add them (Guidelines IV.B, IV.D.2).","aboveMaxText":"Above $18,000 the court exercises discretion; the extended formula printed under each schedule is: age 12-18 per-child amount = income ^ .6386 x 4.8982 / 3.5596 / 3.0359 / 2.6015 / 2.3175 / 2.1083 for 1-6 children; 6-11 = x 0.94; 0-5 = x 0.84 (Guidelines IV.G, Appendix II).","effective":"2025-07-01","facts":[{"text":"Kansas schedules give a per-child amount that depends on each child's age group (0-5, 6-11, 12-18); the 0-5 and 6-11 amounts are 84% and 94% of the 12-18 amount (Appendix II).","url":"https://kscourts.gov/KSCourts/media/KsCourts/Child%20Support%20Guidelines/2024-Child-Support-Guidlines-adopted-July-1-2025-clean.pdf"},{"text":"The current guidelines took effect July 1, 2025 under Kansas Supreme Court Administrative Order 2025-RL-121 (dated October 3, 2025), superseding the May 1, 2025 version.","url":"https://kscourts.gov/KSCourts/media/KsCourts/Orders/2025-RL-121.pdf"},{"text":"A parenting time adjustment can start when the child spends 35% or more of its time with the nonresidential parent (Guidelines IV.H.2).","url":"https://kscourts.gov/KSCourts/media/KsCourts/Child%20Support%20Guidelines/2024-Child-Support-Guidlines-adopted-July-1-2025-clean.pdf"},{"text":"Above $18,000 combined monthly income the schedules print a discretionary extended formula (income to the power .6386 times a multiplier) (Guidelines IV.G).","url":"https://kscourts.gov/KSCourts/media/KsCourts/Child%20Support%20Guidelines/2024-Child-Support-Guidlines-adopted-July-1-2025-clean.pdf"},{"text":"The child's age is taken at the nearest birthday (Guidelines IV.D.2).","url":"https://kscourts.gov/KSCourts/media/KsCourts/Child%20Support%20Guidelines/2024-Child-Support-Guidlines-adopted-July-1-2025-clean.pdf"}],"sources":[{"name":"Kansas: K.S.A. 23-3002; Kansas Supreme Court Administrative Order 2025-RL-121","url":"https://kscourts.gov/KSCourts/media/KsCourts/Orders/2025-RL-121.pdf"},{"name":"Kansas: child support guidelines","url":"https://kscourts.gov/KSCourts/media/KsCourts/Child%20Support%20Guidelines/2024-Child-Support-Guidlines-adopted-July-1-2025-clean.pdf"},{"name":"Kansas: when support ends","url":"https://www.ksrevisor.gov/statutes/chapters/ch23/023_030_0001.html"}],"testCases":[{"inputs":{"incomeA":4000,"incomeB":2000,"children":2,"childAges":[8,14],"overnightsA":0},"expected":1098.55,"what":"payer A's monthly share of the gross child support obligation (Line D.5, before adjustments)","source":"Computed by hand from Appendix II (two-child schedule, $6,000 row: 6-11 = $798, 12-18 = $849; total $1,647); A share 66.7% (percentages rounded to the nearest tenth, Guidelines VI.J.2); 0.667 x 1,647 = 1,098.55 (final order rounded to the nearest dollar = $1,099). skipEngine: children in two age groups; the calculator uses one age column for all children.","skipEngine":true},{"inputs":{"incomeA":4000,"incomeB":2000,"children":2,"childAges":[8,14],"timeWithAPct":40},"expected":878.84,"what":"payer A's share after the parenting time adjustment for 40-44% of time","source":"Computed by hand: adjustment = 20% x Line D.5 (1,098.55) = 219.71; 1,098.55 - 219.71 = 878.84 (Guidelines IV.H.2 table; worksheet line E.1.a). skipEngine: same mixed-age family as case 1.","skipEngine":true},{"inputs":{"incomeA":4000,"incomeB":2000,"children":2,"childAges":[8,10],"overnightsA":0},"expected":1064.53,"what":"payer A's monthly share of the gross child support obligation, two children aged 6-11","source":"Computed by hand from Appendix II (two-child schedule, $6,000 row, 6-11 column $798 per child): 2 x 798 = 1,596; A share 66.7% -> 1,064.53."},{"inputs":{"incomeA":4000,"incomeB":2000,"children":2,"childAges":[8,10],"overnightsA":146},"expected":851.63,"what":"payer A's share after the 20% parenting time adjustment (146 overnights = 40%)","source":"Computed by hand: 1,064.53 - 20% = 851.63 (Guidelines IV.H.2, 40-44% of the child's time)."},{"inputs":{"incomeA":4000,"incomeB":2000,"children":2,"childAges":[8,10],"overnightsA":182.5},"expected":434.11,"what":"payer A's amount under the equal parenting time direct expense formula","source":"Computed by hand under Guidelines VI.F.3: D.5 shares 1,064.53 and 531.47; half the difference 266.53; plus 10.5% of D.4 1,596 (combined $6,000, between $4,690 and $8,125) = 167.58; total 434.11, owed by the parent not paying direct expenses (taken to be A)."}]}